# Sprint Note: Sprint 1, OHSU Simulation Database

**Team:** OHSU Simulation Database | **Sprint dates:** Oct 6–23, 2026 | **Date submitted:** Oct 23, 2026

## 1. Working Software Evidence

- Deployed URL / release tag / demo video: https://github.com/robekenn/OSU-Capstone-OHSU-Database. At this moment we do not have any demos because we have been focusing on the architecture of our product. We plan by the 2nd sprint to have a base website working, with minimal features in progress.
- CI run: CI not set up yet

## 2. What Got Done

- Board link: https://github.com/users/robekenn/projects/4
- Done this sprint: Designed and documented the database schema. It consists of 11 tables. It covers case versioning, outcome mapping, and reviews. This is based on the template Word document given to us from the project partner.

## 3. Top Risk and One Decision Needed

- Top risk: The biggest risk is that OHSU has not confirmed hosting and logging in. So as a group, we decided on AWS for hosting and OIDC for sign-in, but we are waiting on OHSU's IT team to give us a thumbs up. This does not allow us to deploy or test real sign-in until they answer. If we cannot deploy or test it, we cannot show a working, hosted system.
- Decision needed (from whom, by when): The decision we need from the project partner is whether OHSU IT approves hosting on AWS and OIDC sign-in, by [TODO: date].

